From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:12:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: sch_fifo: carry the queue limit into the offload

A driver offloading a leaf fifo is told that a queue exists and nothing else.
The one number the qdisc holds - how many packets, or with bfifo how many
bytes, that queue may hold - never leaves it, so hardware whose queues have a
settable depth cannot be sized by the qdisc that describes them. Depth is what
decides the latency a full queue adds, and a fifo leaf under a shaping parent
is where a user writes it.

Pass sch->limit on the replace, and with it the unit: the same field counts
packets under pfifo and bytes under bfifo, so a driver cannot act on the value
without being told which one it was handed. A driver that ignores both fields
behaves as before.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/include/net/pkt_cls.h
+++ b/include/net/pkt_cls.h
@@ -1063,11 +1063,17 @@ enum tc_fifo_command {
 	TC_FIFO_STATS,
 };
 
+struct tc_fifo_qopt_offload_replace_params {
+	u32 limit;
+	bool bytes;	/* limit is in bytes (bfifo), not packets (pfifo) */
+};
+
 struct tc_fifo_qopt_offload {
 	enum tc_fifo_command command;
 	u32 handle;
 	u32 parent;
 	union {
+		struct tc_fifo_qopt_offload_replace_params replace_params;
 		struct tc_qopt_offload_stats stats;
 	};
 };
--- a/net/sched/sch_fifo.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_fifo.c
@@ -67,6 +67,8 @@ static void fifo_offload_init(struct Qdi
 	qopt.command = TC_FIFO_REPLACE;
 	qopt.handle = sch->handle;
 	qopt.parent = sch->parent;
+	qopt.replace_params.limit = sch->limit;
+	qopt.replace_params.bytes = sch->ops == &bfifo_qdisc_ops;
 	dev->netdev_ops->ndo_setup_tc(dev, TC_SETUP_QDISC_FIFO, &qopt);
 }
 
